{{!< default}}
{{!-- ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  home.hbs — the front page.

  WHY THIS FILE EXISTS: routes.yaml maps `/` to this template —

      routes:
        /: home

  — and Ghost returns a 400 "Missing template home.hbs for route /" if it is
  absent. index.hbs does NOT cover it: `/` is a routed template, not the
  collection index. Deleting this file breaks the front page and nothing else,
  which makes it an easy one to miss.

  It is deliberately a plain listing for now. What a home page should actually
  contain is in abstract/11 and abstract/12 — do not guess at it here.
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ --}}

{{!-- A Ghost PAGE with the slug `home` supplies the title and excerpt if one
     exists; otherwise the site's own. That fork is the pattern every
     content-less route in routes.yaml uses. --}}
{{#page}}
  <h1>{{title}}</h1>
  {{#if custom_excerpt}}<p>{{custom_excerpt}}</p>{{/if}}
{{else}}
  <h1>{{@site.title}}</h1>
  {{#if @site.description}}<p>{{@site.description}}</p>{{/if}}
{{/page}}

{{#get "posts" limit="10" include="authors" as |latest|}}
  {{#if latest}}
    <h2>{{t "Latest"}}</h2>
    {{#foreach latest}}{{> post-card}}{{/foreach}}
  {{else}}
    <p>{{t "No posts yet."}}</p>
  {{/if}}
{{/get}}
